@meeting introChief
// The arrival evening, step A10: Chief Calder stops by your table at dinner, on her day off, for exactly one minute.
// Torres is at the table. One reply, a point or two either way; no wrong answer. The head writer's lines (the three
// replies are the onboarding engineer's stand-ins, kept: they were already right).
title: The Chief stops by
from: Chief Ines Calder
gist: Chief Calder: Torres has you on Monday, ten to eight in the Works bay. Your first job on Tuesday is hers.
== lines
torres-zeke: Chief. Didn't think we'd see you tonight.
calder: You haven't. I'm not here. Day off.   [nod]
calder > you: Calder. Works is mine. Welcome aboard.
calder: Tomorrow you're with Torres. Ten to eight, the Works bay. Not eight. Ten to.
calder: Tuesday, your first job's mine. I'll pick it. You'll do it.
? choice
* Looking forward to it.   rel:calder+1
  calder: Good.
* What should I read up on?   rel:calder+2
  calder: The scrubber manual. Chapter three. Nobody reads chapter three.
* (Say nothing)
  calder: Quiet. Good. The ship's loud enough.
calder: One thing. Nobody thanks the air. That's how you know it's working.
torres-zeke: She tells everyone that.
calder: It's true for everyone.   [nod]
calder > you: Eat something. That's an order, and I'm not even here.
